# Line endings are policy, not per-clone state. The blobs in this repo are
# LF; text=auto converts CRLF checkins to LF and never touches files detected
# as binary. Without this, a Windows clone's CRLF working tree stages an
# ending storm — 260 files of pure line-ending noise showed as modified after
# one checkout, waiting to ride into history inside a real commit.
* text=auto
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
# Windows-native scripts, where the platform itself insists on CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
